  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For a sequence BBB, the MEX (minimum excluded value) of BBB, denoted as MEX(B)MEX(B)MEX(B), is the smallest non-negative integer that does not appear in BBB.\n\nYou are given two integers NNN and KKK.\n\nConsider all permutations PPP of the integers {0,1,...,N−10, 1, ..., N-10,1,...,N−1}.\n\nFor a permutation PPP, define a set S(P)S(P)S(P) containing all distinct MEX values of all its subarrays.\n\nFormally,\n\nS(P)S(P)S(P) = { MEX(P[l..r])∣1≤l≤r≤NMEX(P[l..r]) | 1 ≤ l ≤ r ≤ N MEX(P[l..r])∣1≤l≤r≤N}\n\nYour task is to count how many permutations PPP of {0,1,...,N−10, 1, ..., N-10,1,...,N−1} satisfy ∣S(P)∣=K|S(P)| = K∣S(P)∣=K, where ∣S(P)∣|S(P)|∣S(P)∣ denotes the number of elements in S(P)S(P)S(P) (the size/cardinality of the set).\n\nSince the answer can be large, print it modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of a single line containing two integers NNN and KKK - the size of the permutation and required size of the MEX set.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of valid permutations PPP for which the size of the MEX set is exactly KKK, modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1031 \\leq T \\leq 10^31≤T≤103",
      "1≤N≤5⋅1031 \\leq N \\leq 5\\cdot10^31≤N≤5⋅103",
      "1≤K≤N+11 \\leq K\\leq N+11≤K≤N+1",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 5⋅1035\\cdot10^35⋅103."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
